Stage 4: consistency audit (Grounding DINO). Grounding DINO Swin-B runs over the COCO- 80 80 vocabulary and applies two checks: (i) extras , any detected class above threshold not in the intended set;
(ii) duplicates , more than one detection of any intended class. Failing scenes are discarded.
The audit keeps 85.0 % 85.0\% of the renders at k = 0 k=0 , 75.5 75.5 , 70.9 70.9 , 59.8 59.8 and 51.0 % 51.0\% at k = 1 k=1 to 4 4 , and 46.5 % 46.5\% at k = 5 k=5 ; every rejected render has an extra or a duplicate object.

